  "body": "Part of #290. Found while working #532 (Wire EDM: 2-axis contour op).\n\n**Background:** a Wire Contour (#532) mounts no library tool - the wire is the machine's EDM condition (#531) - so its `Operation::tool` is the empty word (`KindInfo::mounts_tool()` is false for the wire family). #532 taught the doors that create, generate, stamp, machine-check and post a wire cut. The surfaces below still read `op.tool` as a library tool. None of them crashes or posts anything (the program gate refuses a wire cut by name until #533), but what they say is wrong or unhelpful:\n\n- **Program stock sim** (`crates/app/src/stock_sim.rs`, the plan walk): a wire cut stops the plan with `\"<op>: tool  is not in the library\"`. It should stay out of the dexel plan the way a probe and a torch do, by name (\"a wire cut is verified by the wire laws, not the stock sim\") - the wire's verdicts are #534's.\n- **Setup sheet** (`crates/app/src/setup_sheet/operations.rs`, `tools.rs`): the op row prints an empty tool, and the tool table prints `(tool '' is no longer in the document)`. It should print the condition id, the wire diameter and the gap the machine states for it.\n- **Tool list / tool-list export** (`crates/app/src/tool_list.rs`, `tool_list_export.rs`): a wire cut adds a row for the tool `\"\"`. A wire EDM has no tool table; the row should not exist.\n- **Other readers of `op.tool`** to audit for the same thing: `cutting.rs` (cutting data), `fixture_struck.rs`, `fixture_carried.rs`, `operation/footprint.rs`, `posting_index_swing.rs`, `tool_numbers.rs`.\n\n**Not in this issue:** the wire verification laws themselves (#534) and the op / machine pages (#535).\n\n**Done means:** on a document whose setup mounts a wire EDM and holds a generated Wire Contour: the program sim answers by name without \"is not in the library\"; the setup sheet shows the cut's condition, wire diameter and gap and no missing-tool line; the tool list has no row for it. Each pinned by a test in the owning crate's suite.\n",
